  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "When proving the angle bisector criterion theorem, given \\(PD\\perp OA\\) at \\(D\\), \\(PE\\perp OB\\) at \\(E\\), and \\(PD=PE\\), which criterion is used to prove that right triangles \\(POD\\) and \\(POE\\) are congruent?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "SAS",
    "B": "ASA",
    "C": "SSS",
    "D": "HL"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(OP\\) is the common hypotenuse of the two right triangles, and \\(PD=PE\\) gives a pair of equal legs. The hypotenuses and one pair of corresponding legs are equal, so use HL, which then gives \\(\\angle POD=\\angle POE\\).",
